*=======================================================
* Section 9.6.2: Tests for Nonstationary Data
*=======================================================

. xtpurt lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3, test(hs)
  [R equivalent: Im-Pesaran-Shin (2003) panel unit root test — plm::purtest()]
  H0: All panels contain a unit root

--- Levels: intercept only (Herwartz-Siedenburg / Demetrescu-Hanck equivalent) ---

. xtpurt lny1, test(hs) / test(dh)
  Variable: Log State Appropriations

	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  as.formula(paste(v, "~ 1"))
Wtbar = -2.5337, p-value = 0.005643
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


. xtpurt lnx1, test(hs) / test(dh)
  Variable: Log Tuition Revenue

	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  as.formula(paste(v, "~ 1"))
Wtbar = -7.878, p-value = 1.663e-15
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


. xtpurt lnx2, test(hs) / test(dh)
  Variable: Log FTE Enrollment

	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  as.formula(paste(v, "~ 1"))
Wtbar = 0.19938, p-value = 0.579
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


. xtpurt lnx3, test(hs) / test(dh)
  Variable: Log Per Capita Income

	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  as.formula(paste(v, "~ 1"))
Wtbar = -6.8653, p-value = 3.317e-12
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


