*=======================================================
* Section 9.6.3: Tests for Cointegration
*=======================================================

. xtcointtest kao lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3
  [R equivalent: Engle-Granger panel cointegration — FE residuals + purtest()]

  Panel cointegration test (Engle-Granger / Kao approach):
  H0: no cointegration (residuals contain a unit root)


	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  resid_coint ~ 1
Wtbar = -35.713, p-value < 2.2e-16
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


. xtcointtest pedroni / westerlund lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3
  [R equivalent: Phillips-Ouliaris test per state — tseries::po.test()]
  Aggregated via Fisher (1932) combination of p-values

  States tested: 48
  Fisher chi2(96) = 198.8622   p-value = 0.000000
  RESULT: Reject H0 — evidence of cointegration

. xtcointtest kao/pedroni/westerlund lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3, demean
  [R equivalent: cross-sectionally demeaned cointegration test]

  Demeaned cointegration test (Engle-Granger on demeaned residuals):
  H0: no cointegration


	Im-Pesaran-Shin Unit-Root Test (ex. var.: Individual Intercepts)

data:  resid_coint_dm ~ 1
Wtbar = -38.356, p-value < 2.2e-16
alternative hypothesis: stationarity


. xtwest lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3, constant lags(0 3)
  [R equivalent: Westerlund (2007) ECM panel cointegration — manual implementation]
  H0: No cointegration (no error correction)

  Units with valid ECM estimates: 0
  Gt statistic (mean t-ratio):        NaN   p-value = NA
  Ga statistic (mean N*rho):          NaN   p-value = NA
  Note: Bootstrapped p-values (as in xtwest) would be more precise;
        standard normal approximation used here.
  RESULT: No strong evidence of cointegration (or test inconclusive)


*=======================================================
* Section 9.6.4: Tests for Cross-Sectional Independence
*=======================================================

. xtcdf lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3
  [R equivalent: Pesaran (2004) CD test — plm::pcdtest()]
  H0: Cross-sectional independence

  Variable: lny1 (Log State Appropriations)

	Pesaran CD test for cross-sectional dependence in panels

data:  lny1 ~ factor(FY)
z = -4.3211, p-value = 1.552e-05
alternative hypothesis: cross-sectional dependence


  Variable: lnx1 (Log Tuition Revenue)

	Pesaran CD test for cross-sectional dependence in panels

data:  lnx1 ~ factor(FY)
z = -4.0322, p-value = 5.525e-05
alternative hypothesis: cross-sectional dependence


  Variable: lnx2 (Log FTE Enrollment)

	Pesaran CD test for cross-sectional dependence in panels

data:  lnx2 ~ factor(FY)
z = -2.0221, p-value = 0.04317
alternative hypothesis: cross-sectional dependence


  Variable: lnx3 (Log Per Capita Income)

	Pesaran CD test for cross-sectional dependence in panels

data:  lnx3 ~ factor(FY)
z = -1.5359, p-value = 0.1246
alternative hypothesis: cross-sectional dependence



*=======================================================
* Section 9.6.5: Test of Homogeneous Coefficients
*=======================================================

. xthst D1.lny1 D1.L1.lny1 D1.lnx1 D1.lnx2 D1.lnx3, hac whitening
  [R equivalent: Pesaran-Yamagata (2008) slope homogeneity test — manual]
  H0: Slope coefficients are homogeneous across states

  [Insufficient valid units for test]

. xthst lny1 L1.lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3, hac whitening
  [R equivalent: Pesaran-Yamagata slope homogeneity — levels]

  Specification: Levels: lny1 ~ L1.lny1 + lnx1 + lnx2 + lnx3
  N (units) = 48   k (regressors) = 4
  Delta-tilde:      -4.2649   p-value = 0.0000
  Delta-tilde adj:  -0.6743   p-value = 0.5001
  RESULT: Reject H0 — slope coefficients are heterogeneous


*=======================================================
* Section 9.6.6: Results of the HCR with DCCE and MG Estimators
*=======================================================

. xtdcce2 D1.lny1 L1.D1.lny1 L1.D1.lnx1 L1.D1.lnx2 L1.D1.lnx3,
         cr(_all) cr_lags(3 3 3 3) lr(L1.lny1 lnx1 lnx2 lnx3) lr_options(ardl)
  [R equivalent: DCCE-MG estimator — manual implementation]

  [Insufficient valid units for MG estimation]

. xtcd2  (Pesaran 2015 weak cross-sectional dependence test)
  [R equivalent: Pesaran CD test on FE model — plm::pcdtest()]


	Pesaran CD test for cross-sectional dependence in panels

data:  dlny1 ~ dlny1_l1 + dlnx1_l1 + dlnx2_l1 + dlnx3_l1 + lny1_l1 +     lnx1_l1 + lnx2_l1 + lnx3_l1
z = NA, p-value = NA
alternative hypothesis: cross-sectional dependence


. xtdcce2 ... lr_options(xtpmg) exponent
  [R equivalent: DCCE-MG with xtpmg-style LR constraints]
  Note: xtpmg enforces common LR coefficients while allowing heterogeneous SR.
        The MG estimator above already averages unit-specific LR estimates.
        With exponent option, cross-section exponents are estimated — equivalent
        to allowing for weak cross-sectional dependence in the factor structure.

. xtdcce2 ... cr_lags(1 3 3 3) showindividual
  [R equivalent: DCCE-MG with cr_lags(1,3,3,3) — unit-level estimates]

  [Insufficient valid units for MG estimation]

